{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119698","id":3736409701,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7etRZl","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119698","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119698.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119698.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119698","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119698/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119698/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119698/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/0bb2dde2fd3141f4363ea5e32a4a257aaa8e6ba6","number":119698,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"[iOS] Add AccessKit screen reader support","user":{"login":"iMacHumphries","id":10065149,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDY1MTQ5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10065149?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/iMacHumphries","html_url":"https://github.com/iMacHumphries","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iMacHumphries/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iMacHumphries/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iMacHumphries/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iMacHumphries/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iMacHumphries/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iMacHumphries/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iMacHumphries/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iMacHumphries/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iMacHumphries/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"> [!NOTE]\r\n> AI-assisted contribution disclosure:\r\nClaude Code was used to help generate an initial boilerplate draft based on the existing macOS AccessKit implementation and to explore unfamiliar APIs. The generated code was not accepted as-is and required significant manual debugging, modification, integration work, and testing.\r\nThe implementation was built, exported, and tested manually on physical iOS hardware with VoiceOver enabled. Additional fixes and follow-up changes were made during review and integration.\r\nThis PR should be considered AI-assisted, not AI-authored.\r\n\r\n## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\niOS is currently the only major Godot platform without screen reader support. macOS, Windows, and Linux already integrate the AccessKit-based `AccessibilityServerAccessKit` driver, but iOS has no implementation, so VoiceOver cannot read `Control` elements or their `accessibility_name` / `description` / `role` properties in apps exported from Godot.\r\n\r\nThis PR adds the missing iOS glue so VoiceOver works out of the box, using the same driver and the upstream `accesskit_ios_subclassing_adapter`.\r\n\r\n- Closes #\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\n### What changed\r\n\r\n- **`drivers/accesskit/accessibility_server_accesskit.{h,cpp}`** - Adds an `APPLE_EMBEDDED_ENABLED` branch alongside the existing macOS / Windows / Linux paths in `window_create` / `window_destroy` / `update_if_active`, using AccessKit's 3-callback iOS variant.\r\n- **`platform/apple_embedded/display_server_apple_embedded.{h,mm}`** - Registers `godotView` as the host `UIView` with `AccessibilityServer::window_create`, advertises `FEATURE_ACCESSIBILITY_SCREEN_READER`, and surfaces VoiceOver state via `accessibility_screen_reader_active()` backed by `UIAccessibilityIsVoiceOverRunning`.\r\n- **`platform/ios/detect.py`** - Adds an `accesskit_sdk_path` SCons option mirroring the macOS pattern, links the appropriate device / simulator static slice, and defines `ACCESSKIT_ENABLED` when found.\r\n- **`drivers/SCsub`** - Includes the AccessKit driver sources in the iOS build.\r\n\r\n### Scope decisions\r\n\r\n- **visionOS deliberately not enabled.** The `APPLE_EMBEDDED_ENABLED` guard would cover it, but visionOS is kept out of `drivers/SCsub` and `platform/visionos/detect.py` to limit this PR's scope. Happy to follow up in a separate PR.\r\n- **No new script-exposed API.** No `doc/classes/` changes are required - the feature surfaces through the existing `AccessibilityServer` API and `Control.accessibility_*` properties already documented for the other platforms.\r\n\r\n### Dependency status\r\n\r\nThis PR depends on **AccessKit C 0.22.1** (released 2026-05-24, [AccessKit/accesskit-c#94](https://github.com/AccessKit/accesskit-c/pull/94)), which introduces the iOS adapters.\r\n\r\nA matching **godot-accesskit-c-static** release with iOS binaries (`lib/ios/{arm64,simulator_arm64}/static/libaccesskit.a`) is still pending. Until that lands, the PR can be built by compiling `accesskit-c` 0.22.1 locally and pointing `accesskit_sdk_path=...` at the resulting tree. **Suggest holding merge until the static-bindings release is cut.**\r\n\r\n### Test plan\r\n\r\nManual VoiceOver testing - no automated tests added. The change is platform glue with no host-testable surface, matching how the macOS / Windows / Linux AccessKit integrations were merged.\r\n\r\nTested with VoiceOver enabled on:\r\n- [x] iOS device (arm64) - `Control` nodes are reachable via swipe navigation; `accessibility_name`, `description`, and `role` are announced\r\n- [x] Confirmed no regression with VoiceOver disabled\r\n\r\nReviewers wanting to reproduce: build `accesskit-c` 0.22.1 with the iOS targets, then:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nscons platform=ios target=template_debug arch=arm64 accesskit_sdk_path=/path/to/accesskit-c\r\n```\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","c